{
  "notice": "Verb-then-object interpretation used after intent classification (backend/nlu/frame.py). Pepper looks for the action verb or question word first, then for what the request is about. Question words (where, which, when, who, what, how, how many) count as verbs. General request verbs (ngicela, ngifuna, ngidinga) cover every task and rank below every specific verb. Patterns are regular expressions for the stem plus its endings; up to 10 letters of prefixes before the stem are allowed (e.g. 'siz(a|e|...)' matches siza, ungisize, ngisizeni). A pattern starting with ^ must be a whole word (no prefixes).",
